James Rising received an email from Nishat Ferdous Anika, an international student with a strong academic background in Oceanography, expressing interest in joining his research group for a PhD in fall 2026. She shared her extensive research experience, particularly in climate-smart marine spatial planning and vulnerability assessment. In response, James drafted a professional, to-the-point email stating that he is not taking new students this year. He acknowledged Nishat's impressive qualifications and encouraged her to explore other opportunities while offering a chance for a brief online meeting to discuss her interests further. James provided a scheduling link for the meeting.
